  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN207.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">makaṭpōkkiya cevili colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What was said by the foster mother who had let [her] daughter go.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN207.1">
        <l><anchor n="1"/>aṇaṅkuṭai mu<supplied>nnī</supplied>r paranta ceṟuvi</l>
        <l>ṉuṇaṅkutiṟam peyarnta veṇka lamiḻtaṅ</l>
        <l>kuṭapula maruṅki ṉu<supplied>y</supplied>mmār puḷḷōrttup</l>
        <l>paṭaiyamait teḻunta peruñcē yāṭavar</l>
        <l>niraipparap poṟaiya naraippuṟak kaḻutaik</l>
        <l>kuṟaikkuḷam putaitta kaṟpiṟa ḻiyaviṉ</l>
        <l>veñcuram pōḻnta vañcuvaru kavalai</l>
        <l>miñiṟār kaṭāaṅ karanta viṭukavuḷ</l>
        <l>veyiṟiṉa varu<supplied>n</supplied>tiya nīṭumarup poruttaṟ</l>
        <l>piṇa<supplied>ra</supplied>ḻi peruṅkai puraṇṭa kūvaṟ</l>
        <l>ṟeṇka ṇuvarik kuṟaikkuṭa mukavai</l>
        <l>yaṟaṉi lāḷaṉ ṟōṇṭa veytuyirttup</l>
        <l>piṟainutal veya<supplied>r</supplied>ppa vuṇṭaṉaḷ kollō</l>
        <l>tēṅkalan tamaiiya tīmpā lēntik</l>
        <l>kūḻai yu<supplied>ḷa</supplied>rntu moḻimai kūṟavu</l>
        <l>maṟutta cellā ḷāki</l>
        <l>veṟutta vuḷḷamō ṭuṇṇā tōḷē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="6">On the way irregular with stones kicked up by the damaged hooves</l>
        <l corresp="5">of grey-backed donkeys in a row, burdened with loads</l>
        <l corresp="4">by men from a great distance who rise, having fashioned weapons,</l>
        <l corresp="3">listening to the birds so that they may escape to the side of the western fields,</l>
        <l corresp="2">[for the sake of] the ambrosia in white stones that are moved when the elements have dried</l>
        <l corresp="1">on fields that are spread by the dreadful three-watered [sea],</l>
        <l corresp="7">on the frightening crossroad that crosses the hot desert,</l>
        <l corresp="12">did she sigh hotly when the virtueless man scooped up</l>
        <l corresp="11">in a damaged jar draughts of brackish water from the clear spot</l>
        <l corresp="10">in the well that had been turned over by the large trunk reduced to roughness</l>
        <l corresp="9">of the male with long tusks that suffered from absorbing the sun light</l>
        <l corresp="8">on [its] oozing temples that are hidden by ichor on which bees hum,</l>
        <l corresp="13">[and] drink, while [her] crescent moon forehead perspired?</l>
        <l corresp="17">– she who did not drink, with [her] inside revolting,</l>
        <l corresp="16">being one who did not go, who refused</l>
        <l corresp="14">although [we] offered [her] sweet milk made by mixing [it] with honey,</l>
        <l corresp="15">smoothed [her] hair [and] quoted proverbs.</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
